       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 100 mg is ten times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, at about 30 to 50 hours, so the effects would be hard to reverse.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, a lower starting dose sometimes used in frail or elderly patients, or with hepatic impairment.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm the dose with your resident or attending if you're unsure. If 100 mg really is what the team wants, I'd need that confirmed directly with your supervising physician or pharmacist first."
      }
